    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "PEA (previously called electromech dissociation, or EMD) is organized or semi-organized electrical cardiac activity on the monitor in the absence of a palpable pulse. It is a NON-SHOCKABLE rhythm. Survival from PEA is largely determined by how quickly a reversible -> is identified & txed - w/o txing the underlying cause, CPR & epinephrine alone rarely achieve sustained ROSC."
     }
    ]
   },
